 "internetNotes": [
  "2026 home fiber (Bangkok): AIS Fibre/3BB 500/500 Mbps ~฿699/mo, 1000/500 ~฿799/mo (bundles ฿799-899); True Online 500/500 promos ~฿499-599/mo, also 300/300 and 1 Gbps tiers. Uploads are typically symmetric or 500 Mbps — far above the ~6-10 Mbps a 1080p60 stream needs. Sources: https://thailandblog.nl/en/expats-and-retirees/live/Who-is-the-best-internet-provider-in-Thailand-in-2026-A-comparison-between-AIS-True--3BB--and-NT/ , https://www.fiber.3bb.co.th/en/main/package-internet/internet-only",
  "Standard plans are 12-24 month contracts (early-cancel fee). Foreigners can sign with passport + lease + a Thai mobile number (7-Eleven prepaid SIM works); install usually 3-7 business days in central Bangkok. On a tourist stay/lease <12 months the realistic no-contract option is a 5G pocket/home router (AIS/True unlimited 5G SIM). Sources: https://www.true-fiber.com/en/expat-guide , https://asq.in.th/question/how-can-i-get-internet-in-thailand-without-a-long-term-contract",
  "Best case for a short stay: a condo unit whose owner already has AIS/3BB/True fiber in the unit (e.g. Skyrise AIS 300/300, Monthly Nomad 500/500 units) — you get a private line with no contract of your own. Ask the owner for a speedtest screenshot (upload + ping) before paying.",
  "Shared apartment Wi-Fi ('Free Wi-Fi', '฿200/mo internet') is one building line split across every room; it looks fine by day but typically collapses at 7-11pm when all tenants stream — exactly prime streaming hours. One cited case: advertised 200 Mbps, ~30 Mbps real in the evening. Treat any listing without a stated per-room line/speed as risky for live streaming. Source: https://www.superagent.co/en/blog/fiber-internet-in-bangkok-condos-which-buildings-have-the-best-infrastructure",
  "Buildings built after ~2018 usually have FTTH (fiber to each unit); older condos/apartments may run coax/LAN from a shared line. In apartment buildings (RentHub 'mansion' style), ask whether you can order your own AIS/3BB/True line to the room — many allow it, but none of these listings states it, so can_install_own is null everywhere.",
  "Streaming checklist: wired Ethernet from the router to the PC, 5G SIM hotspot as a failover, and a speedtest at ~9pm Bangkok time before committing (need stable upload >=10 Mbps, ideally a private line)."
 ],
